# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Like other learning-based error mitigation methods, PEC with shaded lightcones mitigates the *physical* noise of a specific quantum processor, so it depends on hardware services with no meaningful analog on an ideal simulator:\n"
msgstr "Seperti kaedah pengurangan ralat berasaskan pembelajaran yang lain, PEC dengan shaded lightcones mengurangkan hingar *fizikal* bagi pemproses kuantum tertentu, jadi ia bergantung pada perkhidmatan perkakasan yang tiada analog bermakna pada simulator ideal:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseLearnerV3` experimentally characterizes the sparse Pauli-Lindblad noise channel on each unique two-qubit layer. On a noiseless simulator there is no noise to cancel.\n"
msgstr "`NoiseLearnerV3` mencirikan secara eksperimen saluran hingar sparse Pauli-Lindblad pada setiap lapisan dua-Qubit yang unik. Pada simulator tanpa hingar, tiada hingar untuk dibatalkan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Executor` primitive samples the twirled, anti-noise-injected circuits generated by `samplomatic` on a backend.\n"
msgstr "Primitif `Executor` mengambil sampel Circuit yang di-twirl dan disuntik anti-hingar yang dijana oleh `samplomatic` pada Backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The shaded-lightcone bound computation is classical, but it is only meaningful relative to the learned hardware noise rates, which set the mitigation budget and sampling overhead. For these reasons we skip the small-scale simulator example and demonstrate the full PEC+SLC workflow directly on hardware, with each step of the Qiskit pattern broken out below.\n"
msgstr "Pengiraan sempadan shaded-lightcone adalah klasik, tetapi ia hanya bermakna berbanding dengan kadar hingar perkakasan yang dipelajari, yang menetapkan bajet pengurangan dan overhead pensampelan. Atas sebab-sebab ini kami melangkau contoh simulator berskala kecil dan menunjukkan aliran kerja penuh PEC+SLC secara langsung pada perkakasan, dengan setiap langkah corak Qiskit dipecahkan di bawah.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We run the complete PEC+SLC workflow on a 20-qubit mirrored Ising circuit executed on IBM Quantum&reg; hardware, following the four steps of a Qiskit pattern.\n"
msgstr "Kami menjalankan aliran kerja penuh PEC+SLC pada Circuit Ising bercermin 20-Qubit yang dilaksanakan pada perkakasan IBM Quantum&reg;, mengikuti empat langkah corak Qiskit.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map the problem {#step-1-map-the-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map the problem {#step-1-map-the-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our demonstration is set up as follows:\n"
msgstr "Demonstrasi kami disediakan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We choose to perform time evolution under a 1D Ising chain Hamiltonian. The 1D Ising chain gives a nicely dense circuit structure, which is convenient for showcasing PEC implementations.\n"
msgstr "Kami memilih untuk melakukan evolusi masa di bawah Hamiltonian rantai Ising 1D. Rantai Ising 1D memberikan struktur Circuit yang padat dengan baik, yang mudah untuk menonjolkan pelaksanaan PEC.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We choose to measure the observable $\\langle X_6 Z_{13}\\rangle$, which contains one $X$ and one $Z$ component. This is convenient for highlighting how the SLC bounds treat different types of errors differently.\n"
msgstr "Kami memilih untuk mengukur observable $\\langle X_6 Z_{13}\\rangle$, yang mengandungi satu komponen $X$ dan satu komponen $Z$. Ini memudahkan untuk menonjolkan cara sempadan SLC melayan jenis ralat yang berbeza secara berbeza.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We want the ideal expectation value of this observable to be exactly 1, so that the quality of the mitigated estimates is easy to judge. Mirroring the circuit gets us most of the way there: for every gate in the second half of the circuit there is an inverse gate in the first half, so that the ideal circuit acts as the identity.\n"
msgstr "Kami mahu nilai jangkaan ideal bagi observable ini menjadi tepat 1, supaya kualiti anggaran yang dikurangkan mudah dinilai. Mencerminkan Circuit membawa kita hampir ke sana: bagi setiap Gate dalam separuh kedua Circuit terdapat Gate songsang dalam separuh pertama, supaya Circuit ideal bertindak sebagai identiti.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, obtaining the ideal expectation value of 1 requires the circuit to start &mdash; and therefore, thanks to the mirroring, ideally also end &mdash; in a +1 eigenstate of the observable. Because the observable contains a non-$Z$ component, and the `Executor` primitive accounts for the desired measurement basis at the end of the circuit, we prepend the corresponding basis-preparation gates at the start of the mirror circuit with a `prepare_basis` function. We use the `get_measurement_bases` function to identify which gates are needed and where to place them, while keeping track of qubit-index subtleties arising from `box` annotation conventions, as discussed in the section on preparing canonical basis measurements.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, memperoleh nilai jangkaan ideal 1 memerlukan Circuit bermula &mdash; dan oleh itu, berkat pencerminan, secara ideal juga berakhir &mdash; dalam eigenstate +1 bagi observable. Oleh kerana observable mengandungi komponen bukan-$Z$, dan primitif `Executor` mengambil kira asas pengukuran yang dikehendaki pada penghujung Circuit, kami menambahkan Gate penyediaan-asas yang berkaitan di permulaan Circuit cermin dengan fungsi `prepare_basis`. Kami menggunakan fungsi `get_measurement_bases` untuk mengenal pasti Gate mana yang diperlukan dan di mana untuk meletakkannya, sambil mengekalkan penjejakan kehalusan indeks-Qubit yang timbul daripada konvensyen anotasi `box`, seperti yang dibincangkan dalam bahagian tentang penyediaan pengukuran asas kanonik.\n"

