# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. Tighten forward bounds with quantum speed limits {#b-tighten-forward-bounds-with-quantum-speed-limits}"
msgstr "b. Tighten forward bounds with quantum speed limits {#b-tighten-forward-bounds-with-quantum-speed-limits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We next tighten the bounds by using the `tighten_with_speed_limit` function. The geometric spread of the observable's lightcone is already fully accounted for in the forward bounds computed above. What this function adds is a self-consistency pass that leverages the limited speed at which information can flow through the circuit &mdash; the lightcone grows by at most one qubit per layer of two-qubit gates &mdash; to tighten the previously computed bounds with respect to each other. The information flows in both directions:\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya kami mengetatkan sempadan dengan menggunakan fungsi `tighten_with_speed_limit`. Penyebaran geometri lightcone bagi observable telah pun diambil kira sepenuhnya dalam sempadan hadapan yang dikira di atas. Apa yang fungsi ini tambah ialah laluan konsistensi-diri yang memanfaatkan kelajuan terhad di mana maklumat boleh mengalir melalui Circuit &mdash; lightcone berkembang paling banyak satu Qubit bagi setiap lapisan Gate dua-Qubit &mdash; untuk mengetatkan sempadan yang dikira sebelum ini antara satu sama lain. Maklumat mengalir dalam kedua-dua arah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the commutator bounds to the bounds on the backpropagated observable: if the observable commutes with a $Z$ error on a qubit, then it cannot have much $X$ or $Y$ component there.\n"
msgstr "Daripada sempadan kommutator kepada sempadan pada observable yang dirambat-belakang: jika observable berkommut dengan ralat $Z$ pada suatu Qubit, maka ia tidak boleh mempunyai banyak komponen $X$ atau $Y$ di situ.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the bounds on the backpropagated observable to the commutator bounds: if the observable has little $X$ and $Y$ component on a qubit, then it must almost commute with $Z$ there.\n"
msgstr "Daripada sempadan pada observable yang dirambat-belakang kepada sempadan kommutator: jika observable mempunyai sedikit komponen $X$ dan $Y$ pada suatu Qubit, maka ia mesti hampir berkommut dengan $Z$ di situ.\n"

